{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Yitshar.</b> Why does it count the sons of Amram and the sons of Yitshar and the sons of Uzziel — they being the grandsons of Kehat — and not the grandsons of Gershon and Merari? And it also does not count the sons of Chevron like the other grandsons. One may say that it counts the sons of Amram because of Moshe and Aharon, and the sons of Yitshar because of Korah, because it is destined to speak of him further on, and the sons of Uzziel — Mishael and Eltzafan. But not from the sons of the others, because it does not speak of them anywhere; therefore it did not elaborate here to mention their children. Or perhaps they had no children."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:48.736664578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}